WEBVTT

00:00:00.401 --> 00:00:04.526
In under two minutes, you will add a sponsor and its logo to your contest.

00:00:04.526 --> 00:00:05.626
We start on the map.

00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:09.858
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.705 --> 00:00:14.128
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:14.128 --> 00:00:16.618
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.618 --> 00:00:17.963
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.709 --> 00:00:21.925
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.925 --> 00:00:22.576
Tap Allow.

00:00:26.232 --> 00:00:28.727
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:29.945
See the three dots?

00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:30.493
Tap them.

00:00:32.095 --> 00:00:34.058
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.753 --> 00:00:36.382
Tap Mine.

00:00:36.382 --> 00:00:38.331
These are the contests you run.

00:00:40.009 --> 00:00:42.031
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:42.031 --> 00:00:43.399
This is your dashboard.

00:00:45.281 --> 00:00:46.709
Tap Sponsors.

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.039
Type the sponsor's name, and choose a tier.

00:00:54.292 --> 00:00:56.649
Add their website, and choose their logo.

00:00:59.985 --> 00:01:01.069
Tap Add sponsor.

00:01:01.069 --> 00:01:05.279
Sponsors can pay you directly, and payment never affects who wins.

00:01:07.209 --> 00:01:09.961
To check how it looks, tap See it as voters do.

00:01:11.941 --> 00:01:15.319
Next up: Presenting installer and quote requests.
